## Summary
Jang Dong-hyuk proposes a political reform called 'Party Member Sovereignty 2.0' to allow party members to directly elect city/province and party association chairpersons. The system aims to increase member participation in party leadership decisions.

## Key Points
- Jang Dong-hyuk introduces a concept named 'Party Member Sovereignty 2.0' for party governance.
- Under this system, party members will directly elect city and province party chairpersons.
- Party members will also directly elect party association chairpersons.
- The initiative seeks to enhance member sovereignty and involvement in party leadership selection.


